  "_notes": "Human-authored 2026-08-19 (#173). This pack had no rules file. These rules deliberately cover ONLY each ARTICLE III division's \"Uses permitted.\" section, not the whole division: the goal is the principal_uses marker for _ensure_use_table_rows, and district-labelling the rest of the pack is a separate, larger change. The title fragment is \"- uses permitted.\" with the Municode dash so it excludes the sibling \"Temporary uses permitted.\" and \"Special uses permitted.\" sections -- the reserve holds only 2 slots, so tagging those too would just make them compete. Districts follow the established category mapping: SI-1..SI-4 service-institution -> commercial-employment (the lynchburg IN-1/IN-2 institutional precedent), C-3 service-warehouse -> commercial-employment + industrial-zone, C-4 town centre -> commercial-employment + mixed-use-core. DIVISION 1 (generally), 14 (hillside protection), 15 (flood hazard) and 16 (special-restrictions overlay) are left unmapped per the overlay precedent.",
